   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask where a place is",
   "texto": [
    "Hvor ligger? means «Where is he?». In Norwegian, luger, literally «está situado», is usually used to talk about the location of a site.",
    "To give a brief indication, the imperative is used: Gå rett fram («sigue recto»), gå til høyre («Go right.»). With verbs in -e, you usually remove that -e: å vente → Vent!"
   ]
  },
